in 1997 director paul verhoeven adapted  the story's starship troopers from  robert heinlein's novel  the mega budget film was a total flop  and panned by the critics  if you want to learn more about this  crazy misunderstood satire  here's the ending of starship troopers  explained  the story is set in the distant future  when earth is ruled by a fanatical  government that requires military  service as a condition for full  citizenship  despite that life seems relatively  prosperous  apart from a series of ongoing battles  with giant alien insects known as the  bugs  our heroes are four recent high school  graduates who enlist in the military for  various reasons  carmen played by denise richards dreams  of becoming a pilot  carl a young looking neil patrick harris  is an academic prodigy with leighton's  psychic  abilities who ends up in military  intelligence  casper van dien plays johnny rico a  nameless jock in search of his identity  he impulsively enlists in an effort to  impress carmen his girlfriend  but ends up in the most dangerous branch  of the military  the infantry then dizzy played by deena  meyer  joins the same unit as johnny hiding an  unrequited crush on him  then the bugs launch a direct attack on  earth destroying our hero's hometown of  buenos aires  buenos aires has been wiped off for  europe humanity responds by launching a  direct invasion  on the bug homeworld of clindathu but  this operation ends up being a complete  disaster  100 000 soldiers die in the first hour  alone  including most of rico's unit rico and  dizzy are some of the only survivors and  get transferred to an elite group of  soldiers known as the roughnecks  led by the stoic lieutenant rajak played  by michael ironside  soon after rico dizzy and the roughnecks  are on their way to answer a distress  call on a world  only known as planet p it's here that  the film's final chapter begins  our heroes arrive on planet p and  discover that the soldiers who sent them  the distress signal have all been killed  they find only a lone survivor a general  who explains his forces have discovered  an unknown group of bugs called brain  bugs that have the ability to absorb  knowledge by feasting on the minds of  humans  the bugs then attack the base and many  roughnecks are killed  including lieutenant rajek and dizzy i'm  done  i'm dying however rico and several  others are saved by a passing ship  piloted by carmen rico has given command  to the roughnecks and his old buddy carl  tasks him with another operation we're  going back to p  to capture that brain however carmen's  ship is suddenly hit by an explosive  plasma projectile  she crash lands on planet p and is  captured by the bugs  she's then brought before the elusive  brain bug who's hungry for the young  pilot's tasty grey matter  but rico and a couple other roughnecks  arrive at the last minute and save her  johnny and carmen retreat to the surface  and moments later  they find that the brain bug has been  captured carl arrives on the scene and  uses his psychic powers to sense its  emotions  he declares it's afraid  [Music]  it's afraid the surrounding soldiers  cheer  and the film ends with a military  recruitment video  encouraging the audience to join the  fight against the bugs  after humanity's victory on planet p  it's probably safe to assume that johnny  carmen and carl are all locked into a  lifetime in the military  after the destruction of buenos aires we  doubt they'll ever return to the lives  they had before  they can't go home again both in a  literal and metaphorical sense  the final recruitment ad gives us a  chance to check in on our heroes one  last time  rico has been given permanent command to  the roughnecks  carmen has achieved her dream of  becoming a starship captain  and carl was president the first ever  capture of a brain bug so we can only  imagine the promotions that await him  in the future but are rico and carmen  going to get back together  the film ends with their relationship  status uncertain they each had romantic  adventures while apart  carmen with her crewmates xander and  rico with dizzy  but now both of their would-be paramours  are deceased but there was an alternate  ending that settled things far more  definitively  in this scrapped version of the finale  rico and carmen celebrate their victory  on planet p  with a kiss reaffirming their romantic  relationship  when carmen's ship crash lands on planet  p she radios johnny  telling him there are bugs closing in  all around her  rico hesitates for a moment before  ordering the roughnecks to ignore her  distress call and continue onward  he knows that the bugs don't take  prisoners a few minutes later rico stops  in his tracks and says  she's still alive how do you know  i don't know how i know but i know it  turns out that rico's hunch is correct  carmen is indeed alive as the prisoner  of the brain bug  and rico manages to rescue her but how  did rico do this  we know that psychic powers exist in the  world of starship troopers  but rico definitively doesn't have them  the film does actually offer a potential  explanation to rico's lucky hunch in its  closing moments  but it's easy to miss when rico finally  reunites with carl at the end of the  film  a new possibility occurs to him he says  to carl  it was you wasn't it you told me how to  find carmen  all carl says in return is well that's  classified  it seems that carl's psychic powers much  like his military rank  had risen to heights he never would have  thought possible  on a basic level starship troopers isn't  a difficult movie to understand  there's not much ambiguity in the ending  nor are there any last minute plot  twists but on a deeper thematic level  it's a surprisingly tough film to pin  down and easy to misinterpret  in one sense it's just a movie about  soldiers killing bugs without really  telling the audience how to feel about  it  because of this when the film was first  released it was panned for being  violent joyless and empty we totally get  how this happened  there's no big speech at the end where  our main character says  i was wrong war is bad the humans and  bugs don't discover that they aren't so  different after all  and decide to make peace honestly no one  really learns anything in the end  that's not to say that the film doesn't  have a point that it's trying to make  it actually has several but these  characters in this world are so far  gone that there's no saving them they  can't learn the lesson but  we can starship troopers is a cautionary  tale  trying to steer us away from the  horrible future this film depicts  one of the topics that starship troopers  seems interested in exploring is the  idea of self-delusion  all throughout the film single-minded  obsession and willful ignorance  lead to the characters either dying or  ruining their lives  the humans believe that the bugs are  weak and that victory on clindathu is  assured but then the bugs slaughter  them mercilessly and they're forced to  retreat humans think that the bugs are  unintelligent but at the end of the film  they discover the intelligent brain bugs  time and again  the humans end up being completely wrong  but this theme isn't just explored on a  cosmic scale  it's also reflected in the lives of our  heroes rico's all-consuming love for  carmen makes him enlist in the infantry  which forces him to endure  life-threatening horrors  dizzy's obsession with rico leads her to  request a transfer to his unit  which ultimately leads to her death  starship troopers shows us that many of  the horrible things that happen to us  are things that we do to ourselves out  of pride  one of the central themes of starship  troopers is a critique of fascism  fascism is a somewhat loose concept  describing a range of different  political movements united by how they  gain and maintain control  in his 1995 essay philosopher umberto  echo  lists 14 qualities of fascism these  qualities include a rejection of arts  and the humanities  a need to exist in a state of perpetual  warfare propaganda  and a tendency to characterize their  enemies as both quote horrible threat  that will destroy us all  and no match for our superior military  might  echo states that fascist governments are  condemned to lose wars because they are  constitutionally incapable of  objectively evaluating the force of the  enemy  you may notice that many of the tenets  of fascism seemingly contradict one  another  and you'd be correct at the end of the  day starship troopers shows that fascism  is anti-intellectual  as exemplified by pretty much every  character in the film  and is a system that definitely deserves  ridicule  perhaps a major reason why critics  initially labeled starship troopers as  feeling brainless and soulless  is because of how often our heroes have  to face horrifically grim tragedies  with no warning and with seemingly no  deeper meaning  buenos aires is destroyed by a meteor  killing rico's parents  during a training exercise a perfectly  nice farm boy gets accidentally shot in  the head  and the woman who accidentally shoots  him a kind person with dreams of  becoming a politician has her entire  career destroyed in an instant  is the film just doing this for cheap  shock value what are we supposed to make  of all this senseless suffering  there's an argument to be made that  starship troopers is a work of  existential nihilism  the french philosopher jean-paul sartre  said that we live in a world without a  god  where everything comes into existence  empty of meaning  basically stuff just happens and it  doesn't mean anything  the idea that war and by extension life  is meaningless  is a common theme in war movies  happiness or a sense of purpose only  occurs in glimmers  such as executing the perfect play to  win the high school football game  dancing with your squad mates as a  soldier plays the violin  or spending the night with your  sweetheart before a big battle  when everything seems meaningless hold  on to your friends and enjoy what time  you have with them  because that's all you have in the end  the book and the film versions of  starship troopers share many of the same  character names and plot beats but  they're wildly different  in terms of their priorities and deeper  messages  the book spends most of its time inside  of johnny rico's head as he muses about  life while at boot camp but the movie is  more of an ensemble piece and focuses on  the war itself  also the soldiers in the novel have  powered armor exoskeletons but trying to  replicate all of these imaginary set  pieces on screen  may have been a bit advanced for a film  to handle back in 1997.  in fact verhoeven wasn't a fan of the  book at all in an interview with empire  he said quote  it is really quite a bad book he then  went on to say about  his cinematic adaptation all the way  through we were fighting with the  fascism  the ultra militarism all the way through  i wanted the audience to be asking  are these people crazy if you can't get  enough starship troopers then we have  some good news  and some bad news the good news is that  the end of this film  isn't the end of the story as there are  numerous direct to video sequels the bad  news  they are not that great the first two  sequels are direct to video live action  films starship troopers 2 heroes of the  federation  is pretty much universally disliked it  doesn't feature any returning characters  and it doesn't have any of the satiric  self-awareness of the original film  starship troopers 3 marauder however is  more of a return to form  not only because casper van dien returns  to reprise his role as  johnny rico but because the filmmakers  once again achieve a satiric tone  more in line with the first installment  it's a bit of a step down in quality  from the first movie in pretty much all  respects  but it's still totally worth a watch for  die hard fans  after the third movie the franchise  switched over to the world of animation  starship troopers invasion wasn't  especially loved by critics and it was  compared unfavorably to a bad video game  cut scene  and finally starship troopers trader of  mars  received some lukewarm praise for being  a campy fun time  but it's still paled in comparison to  the original film  on the plus side not only does casper  van deen return to voice rico and  traitor of mars but this time deena  meyer  also returns to provide the voice for  dizzy  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

